1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
is to open your heart to God.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:10,380
To lift your heart and mind to the Father.

3
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:18,580
To partner with Jesus to bend the arc of human history

4
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,580
in the direction of the kingdom.

5
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:27,060
To pray is to do something with the Spirit,

6
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:30,500
and for the Spirit to do something in us.

7
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:35,640
To speak and to listen.

8
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:42,400
To pray is to commune with a God

9
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:47,360
who is closer to us than we are to ourselves.

10
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:59,260
All right.

11
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:00,640
Prayer.

12
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:01,740
That's why we're here.

13
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:04,200
Practicing the way of prayer

14
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,980
is something that we want to instantiate

15
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:09,340
in the lives of everybody here at Canvas Community Church.

16
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:12,420
We want it to become a steady practice in everyone's life.

17
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:14,260
A thing we always do.

18
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:15,460
A very regular part of life.

19
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:16,420
And it can take many forms.

20
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:19,580
Obviously, loud, silent, sung, spoken.

21
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,020
It's many forms.

22
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:22,960
And I know that a lot of people in the room here

23
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:26,900
are at different levels in their association with God.

24
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:30,760
You may be a person that just prays constantly

25
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,060
without even thinking about it anymore.

26
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:33,360
It's just part of your daily life.

27
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:36,960
You may be a person who goes back to prayer

28
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:38,560
to remind yourself of God's goodness.

29
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:39,760
Because it's true that in prayer,

30
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:40,920
when we get with God,

31
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:41,900
we remember the good times.

32
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,840
Just like when you meet an old friend.

33
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,780
You begin to remember why you were friends.

34
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:49,580
You meet with God and you remember when He's come through

35
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:50,380
and when He's shown up

36
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:51,280
and when He's answered prayer.

37
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:55,100
You may be somebody who goes to prayer

38
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:58,900
when you feel like there's just no clear way forward

39
00:01:58,900 --> 00:01:59,940
and you need direction.

40
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:03,180
It's a directional assistance relationship.

41
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:05,000
And you may be somebody,

42
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,880
the metaphorical atheist in the foxhole,

43
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:13,120
who goes to God when there's no other choice

44
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,660
because there's nothing left to do.

45
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:18,640
It's just, and for those people,

46
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:20,400
I want to talk to you specifically for a minute.

47
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:24,020
That can make you skeptical about prayer.

48
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:27,760
If the only time you throw, if you go to God,

49
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,860
is when you're throwing out a desperate,

50
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:32,460
a hopeless word of desperation to the universe

51
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:33,780
because nothing else can work.

52
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:36,920
And it can make you feel like prayer is a futile

53
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:39,620
or a desperate or a hopeless or a meaningless endeavor.

54
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:41,340
And I would like you to take a moment

55
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,400
to re-examine that moment when you say,

56
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:45,620
I need that moment of desperation when you pray.

57
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:51,000
Remind yourself that the recognition

58
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:56,360
that what you've always known to be true

59
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,780
actually is true,

60
00:02:57,780 --> 00:03:00,060
that you're not in control, right?

61
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:04,000
In moments of crisis, I become very clear.

62
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,520
My pretensions and my delusions and my plans

63
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,240
and my belief that I'm in charge

64
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,980
and can make something happen strip away

65
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:13,620
and you have to deal with the facts.

66
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:16,040
And so to say to yourself that in that moment,

67
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,900
I'm taking on this deluded action,

68
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:19,020
that's out of the norm.

69
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:21,480
It's in that moment that you recognize the truth

70
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,260
that you were not in control

71
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:24,780
and there is someone greater than you

72
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:26,100
and you throw out to him for help.

73
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:29,280
You get honest with yourself, right?

74
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:32,000
C.S. Lewis said in a broader sense,

75
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,720
it's in the process of being worshiped

76
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,560
that God communicates his presence to man.

77
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:39,320
You communicate to God.

78
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:41,040
You recognize the greatness,

79
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:43,800
his greatness in relationship to yourself.

80
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,300
You begin to worship him

81
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,780
and then you come to understand him.

82
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:48,320
And it's that moment of crisis.

83
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:50,060
I don't know that God gives you a crisis

84
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:51,020
so that you'll come to him.

85
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:51,840
That could happen.

86
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:53,840
But it's definitely the function of a crisis.

87
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:56,140
It drives you to Christ, right?

88
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:57,440
It drives you to prayer.

89
00:03:57,440 --> 00:04:00,600
And as Ryan reminded us last week,

90
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:01,620
in the Lord's Prayer itself,

91
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:02,860
God said,

92
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:05,020
I am holy, perfect Abba,

93
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:06,320
our Father who art in heaven,

94
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:07,180
hallowed be your name.

95
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,140
I'm holy, set apart.

96
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:09,560
I'm the perfect God.

97
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,580
And I'm still your intimate Abba Father.

98
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:14,140
It's this massive creator of the universe

99
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:16,360
who desires an intimate connection with us.

100
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,000
And we, it says,

101
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,720
are needy people.

102
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:20,480
More than physical,

103
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:21,460
we need our daily bread.

104
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:23,260
We need forgiveness for our sins.

105
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:25,480
We need help with temptations.

106
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,960
We need deliverance from the evil around us

107
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:29,020
and in us, right?

108
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,140
We're very needy people

109
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:33,000
who have nothing that he has to offer.

110
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,860
And that gap is what inspires the worship

111
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:37,160
when we come to recognize it.

112
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:42,360
So those are moments of clear clarity

113
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,380
and importance that can come

114
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:44,280
from a moment of desperation.

115
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:45,380
Don't undervalue that.

116
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:47,760
That moment of prayer is exceptionally important.

117
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:50,020
It's a unique conversation.

118
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:51,400
However you enter into it

119
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:54,000
with an independent and willful being

120
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,160
that's different from anybody else

121
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,040
you run into, right?

122
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,660
So we have to make prayer

123
00:04:57,660 --> 00:04:59,340
a regular practice in our lives

124
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,340
so that we don't forget,

125
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:02,100
so that we don't give in

126
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:03,580
to our delusion of our own importance.

127
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:05,800
That's what we're doing.

128
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,980
We're embarked on this series,

129
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:09,520
a three-year series,

130
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:11,280
of looking at spiritual practices

131
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:13,320
to develop discipleship.

132
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:14,560
Christ said,

133
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,240
follow me.

134
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,960
To follow someone and emulate them

135
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:17,800
and become more like them

136
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:18,760
is to be their disciple.

137
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,000
To emulate Christ,

138
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,420
to build his virtues in our life

139
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:22,120
takes practice.

140
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:25,080
We want to build Christ's virtue in us

141
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,460
so that we become more Christ-like.

142
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,540
So we're going to have

143
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:30,680
roughly three series a year

144
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:31,780
for the next three years,

145
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:33,520
and we're going to have space between them

146
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:35,160
because we're going to talk about prayer,

147
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:36,120
and then you guys need time

148
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,280
to put prayer into practice

149
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,840
and make that an activity

150
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,060
that you do regularly.

151
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:41,420
And then we'll go to the next one.

152
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:42,440
And we're hoping,

153
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:43,140
we're planning,

154
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:45,560
we're going to build spiritual practices

155
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:46,680
into our body, right?

156
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,420
So that the body of Christ

157
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:49,700
takes on the character of Christ.

158
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:50,740
That's what we want to do.

159
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:53,280
Our current,

160
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:56,240
and in this particular one,

161
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:57,440
we want you all to have

162
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,400
a vibrant prayer life

163
00:05:58,400 --> 00:05:59,220
that's rooted in delight,

164
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:01,020
which is what Ryan said yesterday.

165
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:03,180
And for it to be a vibrant life

166
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:04,200
rooted in delight

167
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:08,180
requires not habit,

168
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:10,240
but discipline, right?

169
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,360
A habit is something

170
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:12,180
you do every time

171
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:13,180
because you said you were going to do it

172
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:14,260
because you're used to doing it,

173
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:15,820
and it's bereft of life,

174
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:16,560
but you keep doing it,

175
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,180
it's a drudgery.

176
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:19,580
That's how I'm using the word habit.

177
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:20,800
A discipline is something

178
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,420
that you intentionally go to.

179
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:23,560
It's exercise,

180
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,220
drinking water,

181
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:24,780
eating well.

182
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:26,160
You don't always want to do it,

183
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,200
but you know why you're doing it,

184
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:27,920
and you know it's important,

185
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:28,760
and you go back to it,

186
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,960
and you get the delight out of it

187
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,140
when you involve yourself in it.

188
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:32,600
So we're building those disciplines.

189
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,360
And today,

190
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:36,520
this current series

191
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:37,760
is the second in four weeks.

192
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,520
Last week was talking to God.

193
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:41,880
This week we'll be talking with God.

194
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:43,900
Next week we'll be listening to God,

195
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:44,680
and the final week

196
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:47,800
will be being with God.

197
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,160
Say again?

198
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,620
Oh, you were telling me.

199
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:50,000
That's good.

200
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:50,300
Thank you.

201
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:54,320
And that's kind of a progression.

202
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:55,740
Yeah, yeah, that's right.

203
00:06:55,740 --> 00:06:56,280
We are here.

204
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:56,920
We're at week two.

205
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:58,720
That's kind of a progression.

206
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,420
The child learns to talk.

207
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,560
Later, you learn to communicate

208
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:04,160
back and forth more clearly.

209
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,780
Obviously, as an adult,

210
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:06,740
you must learn the maturity

211
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:07,740
of listening well,

212
00:07:07,740 --> 00:07:08,780
and eventually,

213
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:09,720
with your spouse,

214
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:10,860
you're just there together,

215
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:11,920
and you communicate clearly

216
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:13,580
through presence.

217
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:15,080
And that is a progression.

218
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:16,720
They're not necessarily linear.

219
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:17,700
You don't have to go through

220
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:18,920
each progression with God,

221
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,480
but we're going to tackle them linearly,

222
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:21,440
and today we're talking about

223
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:22,500
how to talk with God.

224
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,660
If we look at Luke 11,

225
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:25,960
Jesus,

226
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,400
this is what we covered last week,

227
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:29,140
Jesus' disciples saw him praying

228
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:29,880
and said,

229
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,920
Lord, teach us to pray,

230
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,400
just like John taught

231
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,280
his disciples to pray.

232
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:34,760
We want to know how you do that.

233
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:35,460
And he said,

234
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:36,440
Well, when you pray,

235
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:36,920
say this,

236
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:37,240
Father,

237
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:38,300
hallowed be your name.

238
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,080
Your kingdom come.

239
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:40,680
Give us each day our daily bread.

240
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,700
Forgive us our sins

241
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:43,180
as we forgive each other

242
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:46,060
and lead us not into temptation.

243
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:47,340
And then he said to them,

244
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:50,880
Which one of you who has a friend

245
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:51,720
will go to him at midnight

246
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,740
and say to him,

247
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:53,340
Friend, friend,

248
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:55,540
lend me three loaves?

249
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:56,780
For a friend of mine

250
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:57,620
has arrived on a journey

251
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:58,940
and I have nothing to set before him.

252
00:07:59,140 --> 00:07:59,960
And he'll answer him,

253
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:00,640
Don't bother me.

254
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:01,380
The door is shut

255
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:02,660
and my children are with me in bed.

256
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:03,840
I can't get up and give you anything.

257
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,600
The word there is actually locked up.

258
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,120
I find it interesting

259
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,600
that they had door locks

260
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,000
at the turn of the millennium.

261
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:09,340
But anyway,

262
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:12,300
it's a longstanding habit.

263
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,380
I can't get up and give you anything.

264
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,380
I tell you, though,

265
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:17,460
he'll not get up and give me anything

266
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:19,280
because he's a friend,

267
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:20,500
but because of his impudence,

268
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,340
because of his persistence,

269
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:23,700
he will rise and give him

270
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:24,440
whatever he needs.

271
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:25,760
And I tell you,

272
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:27,180
Ask and it will be given to you.

273
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:28,220
Seek and you will find.

274
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:29,120
Knock and it will be over.

275
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:29,520
Open to you.

276
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:30,440
For everyone who asks,

277
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:30,900
receives.

278
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:31,720
Everyone who seeks,

279
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:32,200
finds.

280
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,920
To anyone who knocks,

281
00:08:33,920 --> 00:08:34,660
it will be opened.

282
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:36,760
What father among you,

283
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:38,520
if his son asks for a fish,

284
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,820
will instead of a fish,

285
